-- title:
--   Exact per-tape semantics of the complete native LWE row producer
-- statement:
--   For every integer input matrix, finite pool of integer coefficient vectors, rational query and squared width, modulus, cutoff and precision budgets, and one flat binary tape of the specified length, the concrete whole-table producer returns exactly the list obtained by running the certified scalar producer on each pool entry and its disjoint contiguous tape slice. The query and numerical context are common to all rows. The identity is pointwise for the entire table; it assumes neither Gaussian nor independent pool entries and does not take a hidden nearest lattice point as an input.
-- source:
